# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-3 window (octo-T8 and its three levers on the fused stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq arm needs its binary; every other arm runs that
# binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# Q2 (TIMED, the DRAFT A/B arm): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-quaddraft = the octo arm WITHOUT the octo draft: the fused quad drafters draft
# the octo rounds, cut to seven rows on the host. Against L1 / L2 it answers which drafter an octo round wants on the fused stack: the octo draft pass saves one 64-row pass
# of drafting but its checkpoint is trained at 16 rows (tau), and it is the one lever that does not coexist with the draft book (the coordinator rebuilds its trace after a
# rebound member). Estimate: -4..-8 ms of the round against -2% tokens per seat-round (measured on the Lever N stack: the early draft -12 ms against two UNFUSED quads).
# TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ: c2_smoke_check clean AND python3
# scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-quaddraft clean: one "[OCTO] admitted
# mode=live" line, the UNQUALIFIED lines, at least 16 rounds with shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 (the positive control: written after the octo block's own verify counter
# moved), no counted m3 round under live, no program compiled on the first octo round, the K64j geometry line (extent replay engaged segments=8 flags=0x21 ... G8B1) and the
# factory line for the bundle's launch size (entries=4 kv_share=false), and the lever rules: the bundle engaged ONCE (the latch: the warm and the captured fixture build one
# bundle) with its call line, the glue8 engaged line for every site at users=8 rows=8 and 48 layers, no fallback, disabled or fell-back line anywhere. (the draft rule is
# then "no [OCTO-DRAFT] line": a profile without the flag that logs one is a leak); then the pair against the octo arm: octo3_report.py --control-a <L1 smoke> --arm-a <Q1
# smoke> --control-b <L2 smoke> --arm-b <Q2 smoke> (the report names its arms control and arm; here the arm is the quad-draft boot, so a GAIN means the QUAD drafter wins)
# over concurrent8_steady and concurrent8_code_32k_long. DECISION: the default draft of an octo round is the one that wins both tests; a tie goes to the quad drafter (no
# extra capture, no lifecycle code). TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke
# step; read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A gain that comes with a different loaded
# AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-quaddraft
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=70
